# Images: a letterhead in PDF as preprinted paper, a Page overlay behind the content that reaches the edges of the page.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Images · Preprinted paper
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 140 72 80 72
	Styles:
		For style: letter
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Serif
				Size: 10.5
				Line height: 16
	Section:
		Page overlay:
			Pages: first
			Offset: -140 -72 -80 -72
			Layer: -1
			Image: examples/letterhead/letterhead.pdf
				Box:
					Width: 100%
					Height: 100%
		Page overlay:
			Pages: not-first
			Offset: -140 -72 -80 -72
			Layer: -1
			Image: examples/letterhead/letterhead.pdf
				PDF page: 2
				Box:
					Width: 100%
					Height: 100%
		Text: Images
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Preprinted paper
		Paragraph: Each sheet is a page of a PDF in a `Page overlay` with `Layer: -1`, behind the content. A negative `Offset` equal to the page margin takes it to the edges of the paper, and `Width` and `Height` at 100% make the image fill it. The first sheet uses `PDF page: 1` and the rest `PDF page: 2`, with `Pages: first` and `Pages: not-first`. Preprinted paper is decoration, so it has no `Alt`.
			Style: intro
		Paragraph: Olot, October 20, 2025
			Style: letter
		Paragraph: We are sending the proposal for renewing the dining room furniture, with the details of each piece and its delivery time.
			Style: letter
		Paragraph: The following sheet carries the letterhead of the following sheets.
			Style: letter
			Break:
				After: page
		Paragraph: Second sheet of the letter, on the paper of PDF page 2.
			Style: letter
